sux_preface.sh|161|142|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|SolidGroundUX uses naming conventions to distinguish public APIs from internal|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|162|143|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|implementation details.|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|163|144|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|164|145|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Public framework functions use `sgnd_*` and are intended for application and tool|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|165|146|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|consumers.|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|166|147|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|167|148|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Framework-internal functions use `_sgnd_*`. They are effectively protected: other|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|168|149|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|cooperating SolidGroundUX libraries may depend on them, but they are not part of|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|169|150|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|the supported application-facing API.|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|170|151|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|171|152|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Plain leading-underscore helpers such as `_helper` are local/private implementation|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|172|153|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|details belonging to one script or module. Bash cannot enforce these access levels,|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|173|154|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|but the convention communicates intended ownership. Consumers should rely on the|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
sux_preface.sh|174|155|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|public `sgnd_*` surface unless they are implementing framework internals.|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
