sux_preface.sh|178|159|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|One of the primary design goals of SolidGroundUX is reducing repetitive code.|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
sux_preface.sh|179|160|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
sux_preface.sh|180|161|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Common functionality such as argument processing, configuration loading, state|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
sux_preface.sh|181|162|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|management, user interaction, documentation generation, and deployment support|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
sux_preface.sh|182|163|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|are implemented once and reused throughout the framework.|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
sux_preface.sh|183|164|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
sux_preface.sh|184|165|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Developers remain free to override framework behavior when necessary, but most|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
sux_preface.sh|185|166|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|applications can rely on framework conventions and focus primarily on business|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
sux_preface.sh|186|167|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|logic.|sux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
