sux-ui_preface.sh|22|4|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|The SolidGroundUX user-interface layer provides a consistent vocabulary for|sux-ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
sux-ui_preface.sh|23|5|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|terminal output and interaction. It separates what an application wants to|sux-ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
sux-ui_preface.sh|24|6|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|communicate from the details of ANSI styling, terminal width, glyph selection,|sux-ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
sux-ui_preface.sh|25|7|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|prompt handling, and output policy.|sux-ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
sux-ui_preface.sh|26|8|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody||sux-ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
sux-ui_preface.sh|27|9|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|Applications should normally use the public UI functions rather than assembling|sux-ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
sux-ui_preface.sh|28|10|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|escape sequences, labels, prompts, or status messages themselves. This keeps|sux-ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
sux-ui_preface.sh|29|11|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|scripts visually consistent and allows presentation rules to evolve without|sux-ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
sux-ui_preface.sh|30|12|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|requiring application code to be rewritten.|sux-ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
