sux-bootstrap_preface.sh|2|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - Bootstrap Sequence|sux-bootstrap_preface.sh::::
sux-bootstrap_preface.sh|20|2|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionheader|Bootstrap|sux-bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
sux-bootstrap_preface.sh|21|3|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody||sux-bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
sux-bootstrap_preface.sh|22|4|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|Bootstrap turns a small executable entry point into a fully initialized|sux-bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
sux-bootstrap_preface.sh|23|5|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|SolidGroundUX runtime. Version 2.1 distinguishes the executable's contextual root|sux-bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
sux-bootstrap_preface.sh|24|6|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|from the location used to resolve Framework-owned resources. That distinction is|sux-bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
sux-bootstrap_preface.sh|25|7|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|what allows SDK and MCM development trees to use an installed Framework cleanly.|sux-bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
sux-bootstrap_preface.sh|26|8|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody||sux-bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
