management-console.sh|3|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - SolidGround Management Console|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|15|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|16|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Provides a generic, modular console host that discovers management pages at|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|17|4||||normal|||modulebody|  startup and lazy-loads each implementation module when its page is first opened.|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|18|5||||normal|||modulebody||management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|19|6||||label|||modulebody|The script|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|20|7||||normal|||modulebody|    - Discovers enabled console modules and reads lightweight page metadata|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|21|8||||normal|||modulebody|    - Renders a top-level index without sourcing module implementations|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|22|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Sources each selected page module once and retains it for the console session|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|23|10||||normal|||modulebody|    - Allows loaded modules to register menu groups and items dynamically|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|24|11||||normal|||modulebody|    - Builds and renders interactive menus|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|25|12||||normal|||modulebody|    - Handles user input, page navigation, paging, and action dispatch|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|26|13||||normal|||modulebody|    - Persists console layout and framework UI/logging state|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|27|14||||normal|||modulebody||management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|28|15||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|29|16||||normal|||modulebody|  - Modular architecture with clear separation of host and modules|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|30|17||||normal|||modulebody|  - Convention-based module registration|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|31|18||||normal|||modulebody|  - Minimal assumptions about module implementation|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|32|19||||normal|||modulebody|  - Consistent user interaction patterns across all tools|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|33|20||||normal|||modulebody||management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|34|21||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|35|22||||normal|||modulebody|  - Generic console engine for module-defined interactive applications|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|36|23||||normal|||modulebody|  - Hosts functionality registered by ordered console modules|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|37|24||||normal|||modulebody||management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|38|25||||label|||modulebody|Non-goals|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|39|26||||normal|||modulebody|  - Implementing business logic directly in the console host|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|40|27||||normal|||modulebody|  - Managing module-specific state beyond registration and dispatch|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|41|28||||normal|||modulebody|  - Providing a widget-based or cursor-addressed full-screen TUI|management-console.sh::::
management-console.sh|42|29||||normal|||modulebody||management-console.sh::::
