manage-framework-state.sh|15|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Runs framework state actions in a fully bootstrapped executable context.|manage-framework-state.sh::::
manage-framework-state.sh|16|4||||normal|||modulebody||manage-framework-state.sh::::
manage-framework-state.sh|17|5||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|manage-framework-state.sh::::
manage-framework-state.sh|18|6||||normal|||modulebody|  - Executables are explicit: resolve, bootstrap, then run|manage-framework-state.sh::::
manage-framework-state.sh|19|7||||normal|||modulebody|  - Libraries never auto-execute (composition over inheritance)|manage-framework-state.sh::::
manage-framework-state.sh|20|8||||normal|||modulebody|  - Framework integration is opt-in and declarative|manage-framework-state.sh::::
manage-framework-state.sh|21|9||||normal|||modulebody|  - UI and input must be TTY-safe|manage-framework-state.sh::::
manage-framework-state.sh|22|10||||normal|||modulebody||manage-framework-state.sh::::
