sdk-tools_preface.sh|175|156|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Public framework functions should use the sgnd_ prefix.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|176|157|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|177|158|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Framework-public functions use `sgnd_*`. Framework-internal functions shared by|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|178|159|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|cooperating framework libraries use `_sgnd_*`. A plain leading underscore such as|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|179|160|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|`_helper` identifies a script- or module-local private implementation detail. Bash|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|180|161|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|cannot enforce these access levels, but the naming convention communicates intent.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|181|162|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|182|163|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Executable scripts should be based on the executable template.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|183|164|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|User-facing executables should normally be exposed through lightweight wrappers|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|184|165|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|in bin or sbin. The actual implementation script should live in the appropriate|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|185|166|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|product subfolder, usually below libexec, and be invoked by the wrapper.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|186|167|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|187|168|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|This keeps the command path clean while allowing implementation scripts,|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|188|169|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|supporting files, and internal helpers to remain grouped by product.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|189|170|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
